Tandem Source, a web-based data management platform, which provides a visual way to display diabetes therapy management data from the pumps, integrated CGMs; and Sugarmate, a mobile app used to help people visualize diabetes therapy data. The company has collaboration agreement with the University of Virginia Center for Diabetes Technology for research and development of fully automated closed-loop insulin delivery systems. The company was formerly known as Phluid Inc. and changed its name to Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc. in January 2008. Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John F. Sheridan | President, CEO & Director | Age 70 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $406K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 32%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Tandem Diabetes Care, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.4B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +30% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -161% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 50% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $30M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -23.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management h